// An `if` EXPRESSION with no `else`, at a REF rep. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter refuses
// with `emitProgram: if-expression requires an else arm` (`compiler/wasmEmit.vl:12942`, the
// `emitIfExprRef` site). Should print hi.
//
// A MISSING `else` IS NOT A TYPE ERROR HERE — the checker types the binding as `string | null`
// and accepts it, which is why this is a capability gap and not a design rule: the value the
// language says this expression has is exactly `null` when the condition is false.
//
// SITE ATTRIBUTION WAS MEASURED, NOT READ. The literal is byte-identical at `wasmEmit.vl:12942`
// and `wasmEmit.vl:13116`, so the message alone cannot say which fired. An instrumented
// compiler built to a scratch `OUT=` (never the seed) tagged the two apart: this file fires
// 12942, and `if-expr-no-else-boolean-arm.vl` fires 13116. Two sites, two probes.
const x = if true { "hi" }
if x != null { print(x) }
